WEBVTT

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.348
London, baby!

00:00:14.612 --> 00:00:17.137
GUN Headquarters
is right there.

00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:21.271
Let me go in, get the key
and destroy anyone in my way!

00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:23.012
I want revenge.

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:24.535
[Gerald]
Patience, Shadow.

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:26.973
Just let us handle this...

00:00:27.974 --> 00:00:31.281
and I promise
you'll have revenge

00:00:31.455 --> 00:00:35.198
on a scale you couldn't
possibly imagine.

00:00:35.372 --> 00:00:38.375
Come on, Granddaddy-O,
we've got...

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:39.594
dirt to do!

00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:41.552
Suits.

00:00:41.726 --> 00:00:42.727
Right here, sir.

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:45.643
Stone, babysit the hedgehog.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.255
Keep the crab on a low boil.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.736
It's time
for more family bonding.

00:00:56.524 --> 00:00:58.004
Come on, Shadow.

00:00:58.178 --> 00:01:02.095
Got fresh avocados in the crab.
We'll make guac.

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:05.663
Revenge guac!

00:01:13.584 --> 00:01:17.632
Guys, are you ready for me yet?
I've been waiting here all day.

00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:23.246
Sonic,
we literally just started.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.640
Tom, Maddie,
are you in position and ready?

00:01:25.814 --> 00:01:27.946
- We were born ready.
- Let's do this.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.339
[Tails]
<i>Knuckles, how about you?</i>

00:01:29.513 --> 00:01:31.646
I have taken my perch
atop the giant clock.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.475
Now, where is this glass
I'm supposed to break?

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:36.129
Actually, Knucks, your job

00:01:36.303 --> 00:01:38.609
is to "Break Glass
in Case of Emergency."

00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:40.307
Understood.

00:01:40.481 --> 00:01:43.701
I will shatter this glass
like the jaw of a vile foe.

00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:45.790
In case of emergency.

00:01:45.964 --> 00:01:48.663
<i>I will pulverize it like
the skull of a loathsome rival!</i>

00:01:48.837 --> 00:01:51.927
Just to be clear,
the "emergency"
is the important part.

00:01:52.101 --> 00:01:53.755
The glass will beg for mercy

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:56.236
under the shadow
of my mighty fist!

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:57.846
Guys, remember,
we're a team.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.369
- Let's focus.
- Please.

00:01:59.543 --> 00:02:00.718
[Sonic] <i>You know what?
Let's move on.</i>

00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:02.720
All right,
everyone knows what to do.

00:02:02.894 --> 00:02:04.983
Tom and Maddie,
you guys plant the USB drive.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.682
I'll disable the traps.
Sonic will snag the launch key.

00:02:07.856 --> 00:02:09.597
And Knuckles, you stand by to--

00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:12.121
Break glass in case
of emergency.

00:02:12.295 --> 00:02:13.514
See? He gets it.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:15.037
Then we're all set.

00:02:15.211 --> 00:02:16.778
Hologram time.

00:02:18.345 --> 00:02:19.259
You go first.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.089
Tom, it's me, Rachel!

00:02:23.263 --> 00:02:25.091
Can you believe it?
We're both in London together.

00:02:25.265 --> 00:02:27.049
Have you met your sister?
Try again.

00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:28.268
Unless...

00:02:28.442 --> 00:02:30.226
you're not
up for this mission.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.620
Yeah, maybe you want
to be back in Green Hills,
baking sourdough.

00:02:32.794 --> 00:02:34.448
- Thomas Michael Wachowski!
- Gah!

00:02:34.622 --> 00:02:36.058
You brought aliens
to my wedding,

00:02:36.232 --> 00:02:38.060
punched out my husband
and buried me in an avalanche.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.149
Your day of reckoning
is at hand!

00:02:40.323 --> 00:02:41.324
Yeah, that's perfect.

00:02:41.498 --> 00:02:43.935
Okay, now for
her better half.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.507
Ho-ho, my name is Randall,
and I am too much to handle!

00:02:50.681 --> 00:02:52.335
Welcome to the gun show!

00:02:52.509 --> 00:02:55.556
Baby, would you describe me
as jacked, juiced,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.949
or shredded?

00:02:58.124 --> 00:02:59.777
I would describe your head
as swollen.

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:01.127
Let's get to work.

00:03:04.782 --> 00:03:06.436
Agent Randall Handel.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.265
I'm here to have lunch
with my lovely wife, Rachel.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:10.745
[desk guard]
I'm sorry, Agent Handel,

00:03:10.919 --> 00:03:13.182
this facility's
currently locked down.

00:03:13.356 --> 00:03:14.966
Command-level
clearance only.

00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:17.143
One minute.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.363
Tails... we have a problem here.

00:03:20.537 --> 00:03:23.410
Wow, they must have
tightened security
after Shadow's escape.

00:03:23.584 --> 00:03:25.063
I got this.

00:03:26.108 --> 00:03:27.631
You must be new here.

00:03:27.805 --> 00:03:30.460
Allow me to introduce myself.
My name is Rachel.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.027
Rachel Gonnagetyoufired.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.943
Do you know what GUN
stands for?

00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:37.511
Well, 'course. Guardian Units--[mimics buzzer]

00:03:37.685 --> 00:03:40.253
Getting. Ultra. Nasty.

00:03:40.427 --> 00:03:42.907
Do you want me...

00:03:43.081 --> 00:03:44.996
to get ultra nasty?

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.129
Nasty nasty?

00:03:47.303 --> 00:03:48.870
- No, ma'am.
- Okay, then.

00:03:49.044 --> 00:03:50.698
Then go ahead and take
those little sad fingers

00:03:50.872 --> 00:03:52.308
and start tippity
type-type-typing!

00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:55.268
Mm-hmm.
That's right, go on.

00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:57.879
Sorry for the inconvenience,
ma'am.

00:03:58.053 --> 00:03:59.228
Mm-hmm.

00:04:00.011 --> 00:04:01.926
That's what I thought!

00:04:05.147 --> 00:04:07.584
My God,
I love being Rachel!

00:04:17.812 --> 00:04:19.988
- Did it work?
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:20.641 --> 00:04:22.338
Oh! Ouch!

00:04:23.557 --> 00:04:25.994
Director Rockwell seeking
access to the server room.

00:04:26.168 --> 00:04:27.387
<i>Just one moment, ma'am.</i>

00:04:28.692 --> 00:04:31.565
Oh, no. No, no, no, no.
It's her. It's the real her!

00:04:31.739 --> 00:04:33.393
- The incident in Colorado?
- We're still assessing.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:34.785
What do you mean,
we're still assessing?

00:04:34.959 --> 00:04:36.831
- What do we do?
- Quick, change faces!

00:04:37.005 --> 00:04:38.136
Okay. Did it work?

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.313
Who am I? What's going on?

00:04:40.487 --> 00:04:42.880
Why are you looking
at me like that?
What am I doing wrong?

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.795
[grunts] Ow!

00:04:45.448 --> 00:04:46.580
Aye-aye, Captain!

00:04:49.887 --> 00:04:53.064
"Aye-aye, Captain"?
Who are you, Popeye?

00:04:53.239 --> 00:04:54.979
- I panicked! I was panicking!
- Jeez!

00:04:55.153 --> 00:04:56.329
Get it together!

00:05:00.202 --> 00:05:01.638
Okay, Tails,
what are we looking for?

00:05:01.812 --> 00:05:05.163
<i>The security server is
in the 7th row, 23rd cabinet.</i>

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:09.907
Are you guys finished yet?
This is taking forever.

00:05:10.081 --> 00:05:12.214
[people exclaiming][Sonic] Uh-oh.

00:05:12.388 --> 00:05:14.434
Has the time come
to break the glass?

00:05:14.608 --> 00:05:16.479
Or at least break something?

00:05:16.653 --> 00:05:18.438
All right, hang tight, guys.
Maddie's about
to insert the drive.

00:05:19.221 --> 00:05:20.222
Ready?

00:05:20.396 --> 00:05:21.571
<i>Three...</i>

00:05:21.745 --> 00:05:22.877
<i>two...</i>

00:05:23.051 --> 00:05:24.313
<i>one...</i>

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.142
Go.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.364
It didn't work.

00:05:31.538 --> 00:05:32.713
Did you put it in
the right way?

00:05:32.887 --> 00:05:35.368
- Try punching it.
- Do not try punching it.

00:05:35.542 --> 00:05:36.630
Oh!

00:05:36.804 --> 00:05:38.588
Take it out
- and blow on it.
- Yes!

00:05:38.762 --> 00:05:40.634
Oh, come on, Tom.

00:05:40.808 --> 00:05:43.201
<i>There's absolutely
no scientific evidence
to support--</i>

00:05:44.202 --> 00:05:46.074
[machines thrumming]

00:05:46.248 --> 00:05:47.641
Never mind. It worked!

00:05:47.815 --> 00:05:48.946
Little trick
from the '90s.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.514
I mean, best decade ever.
Right?

00:05:51.688 --> 00:05:53.473
I'm shutting down
the outside sensors now.

00:05:53.647 --> 00:05:54.996
Yes! Uh...

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.477
Hold on. Is...

00:05:57.651 --> 00:05:59.261
there supposed to be
another USB drive here?

00:05:59.435 --> 00:06:01.959
[Tom] One with a giant
mustache on it?

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:05.398
Oh, no.
I've got two heat signatures
en route to the vault.

00:06:05.572 --> 00:06:06.921
Which can only mean...

